r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B- Each reco\u001b[17Gnecting clie\u001b[30Gt is told the next sequence \u001b[59Gumber after\u001b[71Gthe\u001b[75Glast\u001b[80Grequest\u001b[88Gthe\u001b[92Gjournal\u001b[100Gkept.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1BResending the saved bid gets back its original \"\u001b[56Gomplet\u001b[63Gd\" answer, with th\u001b[82G original\u001b[92Gstep \u001b[98Gnd order,\u001b[108Gand\u001b[112Git\u001b[115Gdoes\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[7Gnot run a\u001b[17Gsecond time.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B-\u001b[7GThe\u001b[11Glost requests have\u001b[30Gto\u001b[33Gbe\u001b[36Gresent\u001b[43Gin\u001b[46GAda's\u001b[52Gorder,\u001b[59Gwhichever\u001b[69Gsession\u001b[77Gsends\u001b[83Gthem.\u001b[89GSending\u001b[97Gthe\u001b[101Glater\u001b[107Gone\u001b[111Gfirst\u001b[117Gis\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[7Grefused as \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mSequenceGap\u001b[39m, and that refusal uses up nothing.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B-\u001b[7GIn th\u001b[13G end\u001b[18Geach bid ran\u001b[31Gexac\u001b[36Gly once, \u001b[46Gn\u001b[76Gplayer\u001b[83Gis\u001b[86Gallowed\u001b[94Gto\u001b[97Gsee.\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
